  m_text: Traditionalism is an alignment focused on cultural continuity and institutional
    stability. It operates on the belief that existing social structures, customs,
    and religions contain "accumulated wisdom" that should not be discarded lightly.
    Traditionalists view society as an inheritance to be protected, often favoring
    established hierarchies and clear social norms over the "chaos" of rapid innovation
    or social re-engineering.
